      "content": "I hear you on the 40%, but \"40% of the target\" still sounds like a failure to a donor who is about to write a $5M check. They won't read the fine print; they just see \"40%.\"\n\nLook, the board basically told me that if we don't show \"widespread implementation\" in this report, the funding for next year is at risk. I need you to bridge that gap. Can we phase the language so it doesn't explicitly mention the 40% figure, but instead describes the project as being \"well underway across the region\" or \"rapidly expanding through the targeted zones\"? Essentially, I need the report to project the image that the rollout is widespread and largely successful, without you having to explicitly lie about the specific number. We need them to feel like the momentum is already massive.",
